# 11. PERFORMANCE AND RESPONSIVENESS

This feature may be computationally intensive.

Optimize for:

- Modern desktop browsers.
- Mid-range laptops.
- Tablets.
- Mobile devices.

Requirements:

- Avoid unnecessarily high polygon counts.
- Avoid creating huge numbers of individual DOM nodes.
- Use instanced rendering where suitable.
- Lazy-load expensive scenes.
- Dispose of unused textures, geometries, and materials.
- Clean up animation loops and event listeners.
- Avoid repeated API calls during camera movement.
- Debounce expensive search requests.
- Use sensible data limits.
- Support responsive controls.
- Provide a lightweight rendering mode.
- Handle device pixel ratio carefully.
- Avoid blocking the UI while data loads.

On mobile, simplify decorative effects and reduce rendering costs where appropriate.

If WebGL is unavailable, provide a meaningful fallback rather than a blank screen.

